out.update(accepted=True,manifest_files_verified=v['manifest_files'],decisions={r['sample_id']:{k:r[k] for k in ['tic','physical_verdict','full_review_completion','novelty_status']} for r in rows},root_review='Read all ten final reports, provisional measurements, alias tests, source-specific covariance diagnostics, helper spatial/background/timing audits and lead audit. N001/N006/N007 retain sparse same-kind cycle ambiguity and no adopted period. N006 primary published EB is KNOWN, while present physical label is conditional on campaign photometric cycle-uniqueness convention; historical Gaia-supported confirmation is not refuted. N002/N009 have clear two-sector off-target flux deficits, classified REFUTED selected target attribution; neighboring-source candidates retained in reports. N003 three selected windows independently visually audited as steps/drifts/gap structures. N004 three deep occasions and actual P/2,P/3,P/4 covered nulls support rounded 20.450 d, but Gaia period/conjunction tension remains; probable. Read null coverage/endpoints/gaps/noise; lead visually inspected deciding panels, no universal sensitivity claimed. N005 multiple real raw eclipse-like occasions, distinct kinds, broad/singular timing and nonunique cycle counts: probable, no adopted period. N008 valid newly available S105 third target-centered eclipse-like event supports probable recurrence; equally spaced long intervals cannot resolve cycle aliases or Gaia relationship. N010 same-kind intermediate timings favor 56.823 d over neighboring counts, Gaia conjunction supportive, but capable close neighbor remains ambiguous: probable. Unsupported precision rejected; raw extractions use same photons as original sector light curves. N005 S93 near-zero and N010 S102 nonfinite cutouts cannot supply nulls. Catalogue manifest independently verified; unavailable gates remain unknown.',helper_boundary='Fresh Sol lead owns verdicts; fresh Terra independently inspected source pixels and representative shapes/timing. Root reviewed numeric/text evidence without new image loads, requested and reviewed deciding corrections. Latest-sector extraction and Gaia timing are lead-owned.',accounting='Four probable, three plausible, three refuted selected signals. One known recovery, nine novelty UNKNOWN. No confirmed new systems, identifiers, paper or claim-ledger changes.')
(W/'batch01/ROOT-ACCEPTANCE.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf8')
print(json.dumps(out,indent=2))
